On Mon, 30 Apr 2001, Ram Viswanadha wrote:
> cxx: Error: /usr/lib/compaq/cxx-6.3.9.7/alpha-linux/include/cxx/limits,
> line 837:
>           identifier "FLT_INFINITY" is undefined
>       inline static float infinity() _RWSTD_THROW_SPEC_NULL {return
> FLT_INFINITY;}

This doesn't happen when you remove -ieee?  Now that is strange.  I
assumed you meant the linker was complaining about undefined symbols.  No
version of binutils can help here.

It sure looks like a bug in cxx to me.

> 0x20001002aac in ?? ()
> (gdb) bt
> #0  0x20001002aac in ?? ()
> warning: Hit heuristic-fence-post without finding
> warning: enclosing function for address 0x20000524400

Ugh.  Gdb is behaving badly.  This is a shared library address,
however.  The output of "ldd genrp" will tell you which library.

> The program was compiled using -gall switch which, supposedly,includes all
> the debug information.

Right.  However gdb didn't stop in your code.  The shared library may
not have been compiled with -g.

--
