On Tue, May 01, 2001 at 08:42:46PM -0700, Ram Viswanadha wrote:
> 
> Yes, I am aware of that but what I wanted to know was is there any document
> that describes what  "S" means...

This is a compiler dependent and in general may mean anything.  Hence
this name - "mangle". The whole symbol name, types identifiers and all,
it has to be just a unique identifier.  One of many joys of C++. :-)

Saying that - if cxx really follows g++ conventions, as it is supposed
to, then maybe you can find something in a documentation for GCC
compilers set?  You may also have a 'demangle' utility.

  Michal




