On Thu, 3 May 2001, Ritch, David wrote:

> Do any of the FastEthernet drivers for alpha-linux support jumbo frames,
> like many gigabit ethernets?

Yes, the acenic driver (works for Alteon, Netgear, 3Com, Compaq, Farallon,
etc) supports jumbo frames.  I believe that the Intel driver also does,
but I'm not positive of that.  SysKonnect's driver does, but the testing
I've seen shows that the driver and/or card has some problems on the
Alphas that I have access to.

